    },
    {
      "goalId": "2d16528c-1424-5999-b3d2-af4593a147fc",
      "decision": "KEEP unchanged whole operative profile",
      "wholeCaseReasoning": "Fixed framework charge differs from mobile counterions. One Ca2+ replaces two Na+. Under the explicit ideal model,2g at1mmol/g binds2 of3mmol Ca2+, leaving1mmol and releasing4mmol Na+. Mg2+ allocation requires selectivity data. Sodium activity can favour reverse exchange under the given equilibrium model; calcium is transferred, not destroyed. Less Al substitution means less fixed charge; equal pores alone give no equal capacity guarantee."
    }
